    "globalConstraints": "- A plan whose header carries no `**Dependencies:**` line compiles, launches and runs byte-for-byte as at BASE: no `dependencies` key in the compiler's output or the args file, no `addCmd`/`addDevCmd` stamped, no setup commit, no `driver:dependencies` event. The manifest red of Task 3 is the one thing that fires for every plan, declared line or not \u2014 the rule is the point \u2014 and a manifest a task's own Files list is exempt from it.\n- Every new event kind the engine appends to `events.jsonl`, and every new key on an existing one, is named in `fleet/CONTRACT.md` in the same task that adds it; every new shape of an `unfinished` row is named in `skills/ultrapowers/references/report-format.md` in that same task.\n- Findings are about the result \u2014 what the tree, the record and the sims now do \u2014 never about the order the work was done in, the number of commits, or whether a test was written before its code.\n- No sim under `fleet/tests/` names a sibling `test_*.mjs` or `pytest` in a spawn; every spawn passes an env derived from `simEnv`; imports are written for `fleet/tests/` depth (`../run-engine.mjs`, `./_engine_helpers.mjs`).\n- Nothing of PR #1065 is removed: `derive_regenerate_cmd`, `regenerateCmd`, `dropLockfiles`, the fold-time regenerator and `driver:regenerated` keep their BASE behaviour, and `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_lockfile_regen.mjs` stays green unchanged.",
